===Verb===
{{ru-verb|быть|impf}}

# to [[be]] {{+obj|ru|ins/nom}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[так|Так]] '''бы́ло''', [[так]] '''есть''' [[и]] [[так]] '''бу́дет''' [[всегда́]]!|So it was, so it is, and so it will always be! [from the [[w:National Anthem of Russia|State Anthem of the Russian Federation]]]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''быть''' [[под]] [[каблук|каблуко́м]]|to be [[henpecked]]}}
# [[there be]]
#: {{ux|ru|[[у|У]] [[меня]] '''есть''' [[яблоко]].|I have an apple.|lit=Of my possession '''there is''' (an) apple.}}

====Usage notes====
* Omitted in the present tense except in the third-person singular {{m|ru|есть}}, which is used occasionally to express possession or definition or for emphasis. {{m|ru|есть}} was originally the third-person singular, but is now used for all persons, e.g.

::{{ux|ru|Я и '''есть''' тот челове́к.|I '''''am''''' that person.}}

:See also {{m|ru|—}}.
* Negative forms with {{m|ru|не}} feature stress on the particle in standard Russian for masculine, neuter and plural forms of the past tense: {{m|ru|[[не́]] [[был]]}}, {{m|ru|[[не́]] [[было]]}}, {{m|ru|[[не́]] [[были]]}}.

====Conjugation====
Notes on present tense forms:
* {{m|ru|есть}} is the only present tense form used in everyday language. In works of literature, it can be used as a copula for emphasis.
* {{m|ru|есмь}} is only used in philosophical contexts, as in {{m|ru||«Я мыслю, следовательно, я есмь»|tr=-|t=I think, therefore I am}}.
* {{m|ru|суть}}, an archaic form, has become confused with the related noun {{m|ru|суть|t=essence}}, so may occur in formal styles with the vague meaning "is in essence", indiscriminately of person and number.
* Rarely, the archaic forms {{m|ru|есь}}, {{m|ru|еси́}}, {{m|ru|есмы́}}, and {{m|ru|е́сте}} appear in some styles of literature, though they are not understood by most speakers.
